(4674510, 673877, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is fairly well shot.  Something about that blob of yellowish (pickle?), and the wet/gooey tuna is a bit unappetizing.  JMO of course.  :-)  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is fairly well shot.  Something about that blob of yellowish (pickle?), and the wet/gooey tuna is a bit unappetizing.  JMO of course.  :-)  Good luck in the challenge.', '2008-05-02 11:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4674514, 673531, 30049, '<td valign="top">Healthy?!  Looks fattening to me, although quite yummy.  Trying to mess with my diet are ya?  :-)  As far as technicals go, I wish the whites were moved up a notch - seems a tad underexposed.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Healthy?!  Looks fattening to me, although quite yummy.  Trying to mess with my diet are ya?  :-)  As far as technicals go, I wish the whites were moved up a notch - seems a tad underexposed.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2008-05-02 11:48:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4674524, 673890, 30049, '<td valign="top">???  I''m guessing this was supposed to be in the ''Sepia'' challenge?  Bummer.<br/> <br/>As a sepia photo, it''s "ok".  First I''d address the composition somewhat.  This could stand a bit of cropping to show more detail.  Top, bottom, and right could all come in (lose the far right bicyclist).  The image is a little flat and should have the contrast boosted some.  Looking closer at the bicyclist entering the bridge I see some artifacts...appear to be compression from downsizing perhaps?  This photo also seems a tad soft which makes it almost feel slightly OOF.  I''d give this some sharpening to make it pop.<br/> <br/>I hope you consider posting this image to the forums for more feedback after the challenge.  I think you''d get some good suggestions and it would be interesting to see this with a little rework.<br/> <br/>Anyway...best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', '???  I''m guessing this was supposed to be in the ''Sepia'' challenge?  Bummer. As a sepia photo, it''s "ok".  First I''d address the composition somewhat.  This could stand a bit of cropping to show more detail.  Top, bottom, and right could all come in (lose the far right bicyclist).  The image is a little flat and should have the contrast boosted some.  Looking closer at the bicyclist entering the bridge I see some artifacts...appear to be compression from downsizing perhaps?  This photo also seems a tad soft which makes it almost feel slightly OOF.  I''d give this some sharpening to make it pop. I hope you consider posting this image to the forums for more feedback after the challenge.  I think you''d get some good suggestions and it would be interesting to see this with a little rework. Anyway...best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2008-05-02 11:54:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4674716, 672725, 73942, '<td valign="top">you put my kiwi picture (macro entry) to shame, 8</td>', 'you put my kiwi picture (macro entry) to shame, 8', '2008-05-02 13:10:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4674769, 673125, 92309, '<td valign="top">Your going to eat your dog?  Not really sure what this has to do with the challenge? Still it''s a neat photo and I like the windswept look.  The key to animal photography is to always get the eye in focus, they''re a little soft.</td>', 'Your going to eat your dog?  Not really sure what this has to do with the challenge? Still it''s a neat photo and I like the windswept look.  The key to animal photography is to always get the eye in focus, they''re a little soft.', '2008-05-02 13:35:26.000000', NULL, 1),
