(4699545, 674300, 55956, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Greetings<br/> <br/>Hi, I think that this is a good idea but with a very bad realization. The most important problem that I see (always as my personal opinion) is the light. too much on the fruits and too much strong. the colours aren''t very good, not natural but this is a consequence of the light. <br/>from compositional point of view is good.<br/> <br/>Gennaro<br/> <br/>P.S. if you have something to ask me please send me a personal message.</td>', 'Critique Club Greetings Hi, I think that this is a good idea but with a very bad realization. The most important problem that I see (always as my personal opinion) is the light. too much on the fruits and too much strong. the colours aren''t very good, not natural but this is a consequence of the light. from compositional point of view is good. Gennaro P.S. if you have something to ask me please send me a personal message.', '2008-05-13 15:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4699723, 674356, 61961, '<td valign="top">James, you asked in the forums for reactions to this shot.  I like the depth of field, and there is good sharpness.  However, your attractive model looks as if the sun is hurting her eyes.  In terms of meeting the challenge, my high votes went to those shots that you called "food porn" -- because I felt those came closest to meeting the theme.  In this, the food is clearly not the subject.</td>', 'James, you asked in the forums for reactions to this shot.  I like the depth of field, and there is good sharpness.  However, your attractive model looks as if the sun is hurting her eyes.  In terms of meeting the challenge, my high votes went to those shots that you called "food porn" -- because I felt those came closest to meeting the theme.  In this, the food is clearly not the subject.', '2008-05-13 17:18:07.000000', NULL, 0),
